  "enhanced_information": "Chronic use of enalapril/hydrochlorothiazide and simvastatin can lead to potential drug-induced skin reactions, presenting as pruritic skin lesions on trunk and extremities. Skin biopsy may show epidermal spongiosis, spongiosa vesicles, and an eosinophilic infiltrate, suggestive of allergic contact dermatitis or eczema. The lesions are not compatible with generalized acute exanthematous pustulosis or autoimmune bullous disease. Treatment with prednisone at 1mg/kg/day may be considered for suspected disseminated eczema."
